WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:04.480
Good afternoon.

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.980
This is a present from my older brother.

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:11.940
This is... from that shop...

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:15.240
Oh, you came, Touma.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.830
Touma brought this present,

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:19.420
and to think it's from <i>that</i> shop.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:20.490
What'd you say?!

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.260
Oh, it's well done.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.220
That's because I chose this gift.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:29.210
Eh? Where's Haruka?

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.210
Haruka-neesama went to do some shopping.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:35.880
Wait a minute.

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:40.600
I don't think it's a good idea to open it while Haruka-neesama is gone.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.190
Eh? No way...

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.990
Afternoon!

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.580
Fujioka, look at this!

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:01.200
What is it, Minami?

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:05.000
Touma brought us these treats-in-a-can as a gift!

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.540
Oh, I see.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:12.050
I want this all for myself. Sorry, I can't share it with you.

00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:14.590
Oh, I see.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.130
Hey, Kana, you want to take it for yourself?!

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.510
Haruka-neesama, you, and I are going to split it into three portions.

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.610
Chiaki...

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:33.480
What is it, dumbass?

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:35.780
This is a mathematical problem:

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:41.080
Between half and a third of the treat,

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.240
which would be more delicious?

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.460
Putting into consideration that Haruka will be coming home late...

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:01.010
The answer clearly has to be a third!

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.600
Nope, it's one half.

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:06.480
Haruka-neesama isn't coming back.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.940
The both of you can just finish it.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.110
N-No way!

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.980
Listen carefully...

00:02:14.980 --> 00:02:15.730
...with such a scarce amount of sweets, if you can get more...

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.320
I know you want it.
...with such a scarce amount of sweets, if you can get more...

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:21.870
...it will <i>definitely</i> taste better!

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.370
That Chiaki who was in the way is now frozen.

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:36.340
Morning, Kana.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.970
Morning, Touma. You'll catch a cold sleeping there.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.970
Chiaki?

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.560
Hey, Chiaki, wake up!

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:50.350
Hey, Chiaki!

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:53.060
Chiaki, wake up already!

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.440
What are you doing?

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:58.570
G-Good morning, Chiaki.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:00.780
Anyway, that hurt.

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:03.070
You shook me too hard, dumbass.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:05.530
But you were acting weird...

00:03:06.490 --> 00:03:11.830
Although Touma's a boy, “his” interaction with Chiaki-chan seems almost natural.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.880
I only shook you a little, that's all.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.090
Nope.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:20.590
I've never been on such good terms with a girl before.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:23.340
Okay... I'll give you a taste of it.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:26.430
What's this? I didn't do it to such an extent.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.220
You better be more honest, Touma.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.060
They really have good a relationship.
You better be more honest, Touma.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:29.140
Chia—
They really have good a relationship.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.520
Chia—

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:34.610
C-Chiaki, s-stop!

00:03:34.610 --> 00:03:35.980
Hey, Touma, don't touch me in weird places!

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:37.980
Eat this!
Hey, Touma, don't touch me in weird places!

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.860
The weird place you're talking about... Is it here?

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:40.900
You idiot, that tickles!
The weird place you're talking about... Is it here?

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.360
You idiot, that tickles!

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.200
Eat this, and this, and this... and this!

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.990
Those two really get along well.

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:49.620
Chiaki, stop!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.750
Speaking of which, I wonder what snacks are inside.
Chiaki, stop!

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:52.960
Speaking of which, I wonder what snacks are inside.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:55.920
Good relations, huh?

00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:59.710
But... I think it's a natural ability to be on good terms with others.
Chiaki, stop!

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:02.760
But... I think it's a natural ability to be on good terms with others.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.590
Eat this!

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:04.720
I'm unable to be like Touma.
Eat this!

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:06.470
I'm unable to be like Touma.

00:04:07.550 --> 00:04:09.600
Seriously, stop that...

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:13.730
Hey, Kana, are you not going to open and eat it?

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.690
Oh, why?

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.480
What do you mean "why"? Aren't you going to eat it?

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.820
This is something I received... I'll enjoy it alone later.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:22.110
Why?! Let me eat...!
This is something I received... I'll enjoy it alone later.

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.070
Why?! Let me eat...!

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:25.360
Never!

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:25.860
Give it to me, Kana! Give it to me!
Never!

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.910
Give it to me, Kana! Give it to me!

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:29.240
It's so high!

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:30.490
Damn, Kana!
It's so high!

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:30.580
You can't reach the great Kana-sama!
Damn, Kana!

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:31.830
You can't reach the great Kana-sama!

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:33.330
You're so sly, Kana!
You can't reach the great Kana-sama!

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:33.800
You're so sly, Kana!

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:37.830
If I make excuses to myself saying it's natural talent...
Darn it! Really! Kana!

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:38.750
...then that's how far I can go!
Darn it! Really! Kana!

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.380
...then that's how far I can go!

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:48.850
Give it up, people have different talents. What's wrong with that?

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.020
Don't give up! There's still a possibility!

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.390
Possibility? That's only a false hope.

00:04:55.390 --> 00:04:57.230
Give it up, give it up.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:01.440
As long as there's a little hope, we won't lose!

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.320
What's wrong with losing? Isn't it all right?

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.160
I want to bet on the possibility.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.910
My possibility ends here.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.290
It ends <i>here</i>!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.160
It's so high!

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.040
I will not let it end!
It's so high!

00:05:16.040 --> 00:05:16.710
It's so high!

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:21.290
I want those snacks too!

00:05:32.510 --> 00:05:34.180
I'll give them to you...

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.940
Touma, did he really like these kinds of snacks that much?

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:40.370
Who knows?

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:42.520
It really surprised me.

00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.150
Fujioka is really amazing.

00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:50.490
The moment Fujioka asked for it, he got it.

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.240
I can't remember at all what was in this that I wanted...

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.270
...in exchange for something that I lost.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:41.350
I'll be home early, but I'll need to go "that way” to buy stuff.

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:42.980
Where's "that way”?

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:44.650
The supermarket is "that way".

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:47.440
I head in that direction when I go home.

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:49.030
Where's “that direction”?

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:52.990
Uchida's neighbour has a dog that's this huge!

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:54.950
Oh... You're going to see the dog, huh?

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:59.370
There's a supermarket this huge near Uchida's place.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.330
A supermarket that huge!

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:05.000
Oh... It's about the same size as the dog, huh?

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.460
Eh? That huge?

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:10.090
I remember I had a flier for that place.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:12.920
Weren't you talking about the size of the dog?

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.980
I'm back.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:56.680
Isn't choux cream great?

00:08:58.890 --> 00:09:03.560
No, the choux cream part is suspicious.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:06.770
Kana must've done something to it.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.650
Just act like you were tricked into buying it.

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:13.530
If you're scolded by Haruka-neesama, you can show her the board and explain.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:15.030
That's impossible.

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.450
Why?

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:19.530
Kana's spying from behind.

00:09:23.830 --> 00:09:27.750
She'll erase this memo and destroy all evidence after we leave...

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:29.710
Then...

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:33.340
Right, a camera.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:36.930
Since it's more accurate than jotting the shopping list down somewhere.

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:40.260
Using the digital camera, we take a photo of the board and use it as evidence.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.510
We can take photos of that big dog too.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:43.770
No way!

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:49.730
There might've been something more important before it got changed to choux cream.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.980
We must extract the truth from Kana!

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:56.700
What if it was one of those green and yellow veggies?

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.280
I don't want that!

00:09:58.280 --> 00:10:00.620
You'll have to take full responsibility.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:02.370
H-How could you say a such thing!

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.370
She's gone to interrogate Kana.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.910
She's gone to take the camera.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:12.130
What is this, Kana?!

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:14.960
S-Sorry! It was something that I couldn't help but do...

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:19.590
I didn't notice the board on the table when I returned...

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:24.470
... so the words on the board got smudged when I put my bag down...

00:10:25.100 --> 00:10:27.680
It's true that I rewrote it...

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:31.020
...but it was choux cream right from the start!

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:35.940
I thought you wouldn't believe me even if I said so honestly.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:42.990
It's true... Don't get angry.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:47.080
Kana, didn't you know?

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:50.250
My heart is...

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.590
...this big!

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.340
Chiaki!

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.590
Chiaki!

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:00.930
Kana!

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:07.060
The misunderstanding was resolved by confronting her.

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:12.270
It's because she asked... She made the innocent Kana cry!

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:13.810
You demon!

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:16.940
I am not a demon!

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.530
You shouldn't remove that!

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.410
You shouldn't throw it away!

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:44.470
I have something on my mind.

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:46.810
What is it?

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:49.640
Do you hate Hosaka?

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:55.020
It's not that I hate him, but I've said it a few times - he's disgusting.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:56.190
What?

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:00.530
Maki's heart is really hard to decipher...

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.950
It's simple - disgusting.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.530
Before like or dislike comes into play...

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:09.370
It's not good to let it progress like this.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.370
Our club's directive is to make friends.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.170
Hosaka!

00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:20.590
Hayami, huh?

00:12:20.590 --> 00:12:24.620
Hosaka, have you been concentrating on your own romance...

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:27.890
and ignoring the people around you recently?

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:32.520
Romance? Are you referring to my feelings toward Minami Haruka?

00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:37.400
If you're referring to that, that feeling is not romance.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.860
It's not an exaggeration to call it lov-

00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:42.150
You shouldn't be too concentrated on that.

00:12:42.150 --> 00:12:43.280
Sorry...

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:44.900
But it's important.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:48.410
Hayami, what are you trying to say?

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:51.290
Maki's a good example.

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:55.080
Maki is Haruka-chan's good friend, so it's better to have a good relationship with her.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.580
How uninteresting.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:00.340
Because she's Minami Haruka's friend...

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.210
...that's why I should be on good terms with her?

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.800
To get to the King, you must first get rid of the Knights.

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:18.100
I see.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.320
I must start from the Knights.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:23.650
Let's change the topic.

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:26.570
Why not build a relationship with the rest of the people in the club?

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:28.280
That's not a bad idea.

00:13:28.280 --> 00:13:30.660
If I get on good terms with the people in the club...

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.540
For example, Maki...

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.120
All right... Maki.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:38.460
Maki...

00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:40.210
Hosaka, fight!

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.350
Maki.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.810
Come,

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:02.770
let us become buddies!

00:14:04.070 --> 00:14:05.070
Come!

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:10.870
No need!

00:14:20.580 --> 00:14:23.420
It seems I've been too hasty...

00:14:23.420 --> 00:14:25.050
However...

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:28.090
...there are still other members of the club, waiting for me.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.980
Atsuko...

00:14:49.340 --> 00:14:50.570
Weird...

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:52.030
Atsuko...

00:15:11.050 --> 00:15:14.720
Come, be friends with me.

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:23.560
How could you drop all these?

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:25.820
Here.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:44.080
I wonder if Hosaka and Maki have made up yet.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:44.920
Hayami!

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:48.800
Hayami, please be good frie—

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:58.470
What?

00:15:58.470 --> 00:16:00.350
Friendship...

